  "Those rows are listed for you instead of being converted. A unit is a volume on a syringe, and how many milligrams sit in it depends on the concentration of your vial — a number the file does not carry. Writing them into a milligram field would record the wrong dose without anything downstream questioning it, so Dozify shows them and lets you enter the amount your prescriber uses. <a href=\"/en/articles/units-vs-milligrams\">Why there is no one conversion →</a>": "这些行会列出来给你看，而不是被换算。一个单位是注射器上的一段体积，其中有多少毫克取决于你药瓶的浓度——而文件里并没有这个数字。把它们写进毫克字段，会记录一个错误的剂量，而后续没有任何环节会提出质疑，所以 Dozify 会把它们展示出来，让你按处方医生使用的剂量单位输入。<a href=\"/en/articles/units-vs-milligrams\">为什么没有统一的换算 →</a>",
